// =============================================================================================
// The dependency call breakdown — where a request's time actually goes.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS ANSWERS THAT THE LATENCY QUERY CANNOT
//
// 01-latency-percentiles says POST /api/quotes has a p99 of 400 ms. It cannot say whether that
// is 400 ms of application code, one slow database write, or forty fast ones.
//
// That distinction is the whole investigation. "The endpoint is slow" has no fix; "the endpoint
// issues 40 queries where it needs 2" has an obvious one. An N+1 query problem is invisible in
// request telemetry and unmistakable here — `callsPerOperation` climbs while `p50` stays low.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE `type` COLUMN IS THE INTERESTING ONE
//
// Grouping by it separates the tiers of "API -> worker -> DB" without any knowledge of the code:
//
//   SQL / sqlite                 EF Core spans. The DB tier.
//   Azure Service Bus / Queue    the broker hop, emitted by the Azure SDK.
//   Http                         the outbound dependency the Day 22 Polly pipeline wraps.
//   InProc                       spans this application raised itself, e.g. outbox.publish.
//
// Splitting by cloud_RoleName as well is what makes the API and the worker separable. The same
// database is touched by both — the API writing quotes and outbox rows, the worker marking them
// published — and merging the two would produce a database latency figure belonging to neither.
// =============================================================================================

dependencies
| where timestamp > ago(1h)

| summarize
    calls        = count(),
    failures     = countif(success == false),
    p50          = round(percentile(duration, 50), 1),
    p99          = round(percentile(duration, 99), 1),
    totalMs      = round(sum(duration), 0),
    operations   = dcount(operation_Id)
  by role = cloud_RoleName, type, target, name = tostring(split(name, ' ')[0])

// Calls per traced operation. This is the N+1 detector: a value of 1-2 is a request doing what
// it looks like it does, and 40 is a loop that should have been a join.
| extend callsPerOperation = round(todouble(calls) / iff(operations == 0, 1.0, todouble(operations)), 1)

// Total time, not average time, is what identifies the dependency worth optimising. A 2 ms call
// made 5,000 times costs more than a 500 ms call made twice, and only this column shows it.
| project role, type, target, name, calls, operations, callsPerOperation, p50, p99, totalMs, failures
| order by totalMs desc
